      "id": "claim_44c13fb2fc144e5fbcebb900746c988d",
      "statement": "FI-US-MUNI-CREDIT edition 2025-06, published 2025-06-12 and applicable to positions taken on or after 2025-07-01, recommends a two- to four-percentage-point taxable-fixed-income municipal overweight funded from investment-grade corporate credit and concentrated in high-yield and lower-investment-grade private-activity bonds.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://research/FI/US/MUNI-CREDIT/2025-06.md#L12-L20",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aa104d94860f811ab98407c0e68633047a34141fb44a9af7b01d536d67f8538e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8608a3e06dc84da2b61d0e6c2d05b769",
      "statement": "The 2025-06 private-activity recommendation is load-bearingly an after-tax, top-federal-bracket view: a phase-out reduction that draws materially more holders into AMT means M.1 does not survive, while credit fundamentals alone support only neutral to modest overweight.",
      "evidence": [
